 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-04",
  "asof": "2026-09-07 09:59 UTC",
  "headline": "Waller takes September off the table \u2014 and yesterday's Palantir story turns out to be a Google story",
  "standfirst": "Fed governor Christopher Waller said he would \"support keeping rates unchanged\" if inflation continues to cool, and the September hike went from the market's base case to a coin flip: 54% hike against 46% hold, down from roughly two-thirds on Wednesday. Everything repriced at once \u2014 S&P +1.06% to 7,747.71, Nasdaq +1.40%, Dow +1.18%, gold up $125.30 to 4,539.90 in its largest single-day gain of the conflict, the dollar down 0.58% and the VIX to 14.32. A correction to yesterday's edition, and it matters: Palantir's 5.81% fall on Wednesday was not valuation and profit-taking. It was Google. Alphabet's DeepMind released Gemini 3.8 Flash Cyber under a government-and-critical-infrastructure-only access programme, and the market read it as a hyperscaler walking into Palantir's defence stronghold. On Thursday Palantir answered with a PwC partnership and took the whole loss back, +7.71% to 182.53. Two positions in this book are now on opposite sides of the same trade.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "The war \u00b7 US\u2013Iran",
    "right": "campaign \u00b7 Trump rejects diplomacy \u00b7 Iran claims 18 dead \u00b7 86 vessels redirected \u00b7 crude flat",
    "title": "The rhetoric escalates and the price does not",
    "items": [
     {
      "tone": "war-diplomacy",
      "tag": "DIPLOMACY",
      "html": "<b>Trump dismisses negotiation outright: \"I think an agreement with them isn't worth the paper it's written on\"</b>. This closes, at least rhetorically, the off-ramp Pezeshkian had been holding open \u2014 the June memorandum both sides kept citing. Trump added that further Iranian retaliation would be met \"much harder\" and threatened complete elimination if attacks continue. Tehran had spent the week touting a proposal to reopen the strait; the White House is no longer pretending to be interested.",
      "when": "CBS News \u00b7 2026-09-03"
     },
     {
      "tone": "war-casualties",
      "tag": "CASUALTIES",
      "html": "<b>Iran reports 18 killed and 108 wounded; Vance says he is \"extremely skeptical\" the strike hit a wedding</b>. The vice president cited Iran's record on media reporting, acknowledged the military is investigating, and said civilians are not intentional targets. Whatever the forensics conclude, the political effect is already priced into Iranian domestic politics rather than into oil, which is the distinction that matters for the book.",
      "when": "CBS News \u00b7 NPR \u00b7 2026-09-03"
     },
     {
      "tone": "war-escalation",
      "tag": "ESCALATION",
      "html": "<b>Iran's First Vice President warns of \"dark months ahead\" for the US economy and a shift to \"asymmetric\" and \"multilayered\" tactics</b>. Iran claimed new strikes on US bases in Kuwait and the UAE; a US official said no American facilities were impacted. \"Asymmetric\" is the word to watch \u2014 it means the next attempt is unlikely to be a ballistic missile that Jordan intercepts. The US Navy has now redirected 86 commercial vessels under the blockade.",
      "when": "CBS News \u00b7 2026-09-03"
     },
     {
      "tone": "war-oil",
      "tag": "OIL",
      "html": "<b>WTI +0.29 to 91.30 and Brent \u22120.11 to 95.52 \u2014 crude went nowhere on the loudest day of the war</b>. US pump prices are averaging $4.14 a gallon, which is the real political constraint and the reason this cannot run indefinitely. But the futures market has stopped reacting to headlines, because the escort operation keeps demonstrating throughput and because Waller just removed the channel through which oil was hurting equities.",
      "when": "Investrade \u00b7 CBS News \u00b7 2026-09-03"
     }
    ],
    "note": "Three days ago the chain ran strait \u2192 oil \u2192 inflation \u2192 Fed, and every link fired. On Thursday the last link was cut: Waller made the September decision about CPI rather than crude, so a barrel of oil no longer converts directly into a rate hike. That is why the tape could rally 1% while the president declared diplomacy worthless. The war has not become less dangerous \u2014 \"asymmetric\" and \"dark months ahead\" are threats to widen it, and $4.14 gasoline is a clock \u2014 it has become less financially transmissible for the next two weeks. The thing that would restore the transmission is a successful attack on an escorted convoy. Nothing else on the board does it."
   }
  ],
  "ondeck": "<b>CPI release</b> in 7 days \u2014 08:30 ET. The regime's tightest gate is CPI y/y.",
